## Context

Found by the #602 gaze (raid 207-325-327): its simplify phase had to apply
fixes via Bash because `scripts/pretooluse-worktree-path-guard.sh` denied
Edit/Write into the `review-*` worktree, while the gaze skill documentation
states `review-*` worktrees are whitelisted (ticket 0300). Either the guard
lost the whitelist or the skill doc overstates it — the two contradict.

## Relevant files

- `scripts/pretooluse-worktree-path-guard.sh` — the denying guard
- `skills/gaze/SKILL.md` — the whitelist claim (ticket 0300 lineage)
- `tickets/closed/0300-*.erg` — original whitelist decision

## Actions

1. Reproduce: attempt an Edit into a `review-*` worktree path under the
   guard; capture the denial.
2. Decide which side is right (guard behavior vs doc claim) against 0300's
   original decision; fix the loser.
3. Regression: an adherence or integration test pinning the agreed behavior.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Guard behavior and gaze SKILL.md agree on review-* worktrees
- [ ] Test pins the agreed behavior (proven RED on the pre-fix state)
